# seat-ui — round 7 working notes (write-as-you-go)

Seat: UI composition. Build: commit 984a0f17, frozen.

## F1 (confirmed by measurement) — the board's right margin is 110px of dead white at 1920

`.board` is `display:grid` with `grid-template-columns: 372px 372px 372px 172px 372px`
at 1920 (measured). Full lanes clamp at 372px; the empty WAITING lane collapses to
`var(--rail)` = 172px (deliberate, documented at _gate-suite.html:1833-1841). The 200px
that collapse hands back is never redistributed.

Measured, viewport → (board content right, last tray right, gap):
- 1810 → 1776 / 1776 / **0**
- 1850 → 1816 / 1776 / **40**
- 1920 → 1886 / 1776 / **110**   ← the canonical shot width
- 2048 → 1995 / 1795 / **200**
- 2560 → 2251 / 2051 / **200** (capped: the sheet's own max-width takes over)

tasks.dense (no empty lane) fills to the content edge at every width — gap 0 everywhere.
So the defect is specific to the shipped board state, which is exactly the state that is
screenshotted, demoed and shown to Orla.

Consequence: at 1920 the board's own optical margins are 16px left / 126px right.

### F1 alignment contract (measured, tasks.board, .headActions right vs last card right)
| vw | head/Show right | last card right | break |
|---|---|---|---|
|1280|1234|1234|0|
|1440|1394|1394|0|
|1600|1554|1554|0|
|1750|1704|1704|0|
|1810|1764|1764|0|
|1850|1804|1764|**40**|
|1920|1874|1764|**110**|
|2048|1983|1783|**200**|

Left edge (wordmark ↔ first card) is 128 at every width — perfect. So the surface
holds a single right-hand edge from 1280 to 1810 and abandons it above.
Notes (head 1561 = paperStack 1531 + inset, stack centred on sheet centre 1001) and
Timeline (tl-stage centred, 140→1862) both stay centred at 1920. Only Tasks drifts.
Second-order: the dock is centred on the SHEET (816.1→1185.9, centre 1001) but the
board's occupied area is 116→1776, centre 946 — so at 1920 the one floating object on
the sheet sits 55px off the optical centre of the thing it floats over.

The CSS's own comment (line ~1805) states the intent: "An empty lane on a populated
board is a rail rather than a fifth of the sheet ... **and the four lanes with work in
them take the room**." Above 1810 they do not; the room becomes dead white.

FIX, verified by injection — one declaration beside the five existing `:has()` rules:
```css
[data-app="tasks"] .board:not([data-filtered]):not([data-blank]):has(> .tray[data-empty]) {
  --lane: minmax(196px, 422px);   /* 372 + (372-172)/4 */
}
```
Measured after injection: break 0 at 1200/1280/1440/1810/1920/2048/2560; no new
horizontal scroll at any width; tracks at 1920 become 399.5 399.5 399.5 172 399.5.

## F2 (confirmed by screenshot + measurement) — the list's last row is eaten by the dock

`.board.listBoard` reserves `padding-bottom: 28px`. `.board` (the card board) reserves
`padding: 0 16px 84px`. The dock is 48px tall sitting 18px off the sheet's foot, so its
band is 66px + shadow. 28px is not enough.

At 768x1000, tasks.board (the LIST is the view below 1199), scrolled to the true end of
the scroller (scrollTop = scrollHeight, nothing further to reveal):
- dock band  y 922 → 970, x 237 → 607
- last row   y 917 → 953  ("Send registrar paperwork two weeks before the date")
The final task's title and its owner's name sit entirely inside the dock's box. Screenshot
_zz-list-end-768.png shows the tick, the DONE pip and the 2 Jul pill surviving either side
of the dock with the person's words gone.

Reproduced identically at 900x1000. Board states at 1280/1920 are clean (84px reserve).
Notes is clean at 390/768/1280/1920.
